    {
      "parameters": {
        "sendTo": "ops-team@yourbank.example",
        "subject": "=Nightly maintenance: {{ $json.failureCount }} of {{ $json.checked }} jobs failed",
        "emailType": "text",
        "message": "=Tonight's scheduled maintenance did not complete cleanly. The reconciliation\nitself is reported separately; this covers the other jobs on the same run.\n\nWHAT FAILED\n{{ $json.failures }}\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\n- sweep_outstanding_debts collects money customers owe the bank after an\n  upheld dispute. If it is failing, those debts are not being collected.\n- accrue_monthly_interest pays savings interest. If it is failing, customers\n  are not being paid what they are owed. It is safe to re-run: the accrual is\n  keyed on (account, period) and will not pay a month twice.\n- expire_stale_ops_approvals and expire_stale_minor_account_requests clear\n  requests nobody answered. If they are failing, stale requests stay open.\n- promote_minors_to_adult converts an account on the holder's 18th birthday.\n  If it is failing, a customer who turned 18 still cannot move their own money.\n\nThese jobs are idempotent and can be re-run by hand against Supabase once the\ncause is fixed. Nothing is lost by a missed night, but nothing catches up on\nits own either.",
        "options": {
          "appendAttribution": false
        }
      },
      "id": "5a8e0f14-6d93-4b28-9c71-3e2ab7f60d19",
      "name": "Alert Ops - Nightly Maintenance Failed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        1856,
        700
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "gmailOAuth2": {
          "id": "IrWmPXzOkHIt9fdU",
          "name": "Gmail account"
        }
      }
